---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import Img from '../../components/Img.astro';
---
<CaseLayout
  slug="textiles"
  section="playground"
  eyebrow="Surface design + textiles course"
  title="Textiles + Print Design"
  summary="Two repeat prints, taken from mood board to palette to colorways to a final garment mockup."
  hero="/images/textiles/creamsicle-bodice.webp"
  heroAlt="Creamsicle geometric print as a bodice on a dress form and on a model"
  snapshot={[
    ['Course', 'Surface design + textiles'],
    ['Practices', 'Crochet, knitwear, tapestry, dye'],
    ['Medium', 'Digital repeat prints'],
    ['Output', '2 prints, 1 bodice concept'],
  ]}
>
  <section id="course" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="The course">The course</h2>
    <p>
      My surface design and textiles course explores craftsmanship across a wide range of material practices: crochet,
      knitwear, tapestry, dye techniques, and experiments with non-traditional materials. It’s all about texture,
      structure, and form through hands-on making, and it’s shaped a design approach grounded in material curiosity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="creamsicle" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Creamsicle print">Print 1: Creamsicle</h2>
    <p>
      A loud, joyful geometric print paying homage to designer Matty Bovan. It pulls from 60s and 70s shapes, plaid,
      and the color of a creamsicle.
    </p>
    <figure class="figure wide"><Img src="/images/textiles/creamsicle-moodboard.webp" alt="Mood board with Matty Bovan looks, retro geometric patterns, plaid, a creamsicle, and an aqua to orange palette" /><figcaption>Mood board.</figcaption></figure>

    <h3>Who it’s for</h3>
    <p>This is where the marketer in me showed up. Before the colorways, I defined the customer.</p>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="feature"><h3>Core consumer</h3><p>18 to 30, expressive and curious. Builds outfits from thrifted pieces, handmade elements, and unique prints.</p></div>
      <div class="feature"><h3>Psychographics</h3><p>Clashing colors, silhouettes that feel alive, and “too much” in a good way. Nostalgia and play guide their style.</p></div>
      <div class="feature"><h3>Why they buy</h3><p>Prints that feel collectible and emotional, and remind them of a 90s and early-2000s childhood.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Market tier: experimental designer. Geographic focus: NYC, LA, London, Seoul, and anywhere with strong art, music, and DIY culture.</p>

    <figure class="figure wide"><Img src="/images/textiles/creamsicle-colorways.webp" alt="Three colorways in pink, burgundy and jewel tones, beside the final creamsicle orange, aqua and cream version" /><figcaption>Three colorways, and the final creamsicle version on the right.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="grid-2 wide">
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/textiles/creamsicle-bodice.webp" alt="The final print on a bodice, shown on a dress form and on a model" /><figcaption>Intended use: a bodice.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/textiles/creamsicle-bodice-flat.webp" alt="The printed bodice shown flat against a gray wall" /><figcaption>The final bodice mockup.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bead" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Bead curtain print">Print 2: The bead curtain</h2>
    <p>
      An illustrated jazz singer in a red gown, lit by a spotlight and framed by hanging mid-century bead strands on a
      marbled ground. The beads became the repeat.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2 wide">
      <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/textiles/bead-singer.webp" alt="Illustration of a jazz singer in a red gown at a microphone, framed by hanging bead strands" /></figure>
      <div>
        <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/textiles/bead-mockups.webp" alt="Design mockups of the bead strand repeat on a marbled ground and on black" /><figcaption>The bead repeat, on marble and on black.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="figure"><Img src="/images/textiles/bead-palettes.webp" alt="Two color palettes, icy aqua to muted teal and pale amber to spicy paprika, with matching colorways" /><figcaption>Palettes: Icy Aqua, Pearl Aqua, Muted Teal / Pale Amber, Sunlit Clay, Spicy Paprika.</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>
